## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical reasoning on per-tenant quotas, config hot-reload via Docker Config, and lightweight canary routing in a docker-dca cluster.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for runtime config delivery
- Lightweight sidecar pattern for per-tenant quotas
- Token-bucket rate limiting per tenant
- Canary routing and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simplified quota sidecar sketch (pseudo)
const quotas = loadYamlFromConfig('quotas.yaml');
let buckets = {};

function handle(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Tenant required');
  const q = quotas[tenant] || quotas.default;
  const now = Date.now();
  let b = buckets[tenant] || { tokens: q.limit, last: now };
  const elapsed = Math.max(0, now - b.last);
  b.tokens = Math.min(q.limit, b.tokens + (elapsed * (q.refillRate || 1)));
  b.last = now;
  if(b.tokens < 1){ return res.status(429).send('Quota exceeded'); }
  b.tokens -= 1;
  buckets[tenant] = b;
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test quota correctness across tenants?
- How would you handle config validation errors and rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design distributed feature-flag propagation with per-tenant isolation across data centers. It covers Docker Config for tenant flags, per-tenant in-process caching with TTL, Redis Pub/Sub for invalidation and cross-DC propagation, and edge security with TLS termination at Traefik.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for tenant-specific flag storage
- Per-tenant in-process cache with configurable TTL
- Redis Pub/Sub for cache invalidation and propagation
- Lightweight policy/flag service coordinating across DCs
- TLS termination at Traefik edge proxy

## Code Example
```javascript
class FlagCache {
  constructor(redis, ttlSeconds = 120) {
    this.cache = new Map();
    this.ttlSeconds = ttlSeconds;
    this.redis = redis;

    redis.subscribe('tenant-flags', (err, count) => {
      if (err) console.error('Subscribe error:', err);
    });

    redis.on('message', (channel, message) => {
      if (channel === 'tenant-flags') {
        const { tenantId } = JSON.parse(message);
        this.cache.delete(tenantId);
      }
    });
  }

  async getFlag(tenantId, feature) {
    const key = `${tenantId}:${feature}`;
    const entry = this.cache.get(key);

    if (entry && Date.now() < entry.expiresAt) {
      return entry.value;
    }

    const value = await this.redis.hget(`flags:${tenantId}`, feature);
    this.cache.set(key, { value: JSON.parse(value), expiresAt: Date.now() + this.ttlSeconds * 1000 });
    return JSON.parse(value);
  }
}
```
